WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.920
Sanji has the best character arc in One Piece
and I will proof to you why.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.099
So I've kinda reached the point, where I feel
like Sanji is THE most controversially discussed

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:17.920
character in all of One Piece - which, let's
be honest, really says something. I mean basically,

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.830
every Twitter or reddit post and every YouTube
comment section basically look like this.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.510
[insert meme] Except for you. Love you guys.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:32.290
Anyways, even amongst the dumpster fire that
is large parts of the community, the Sanji

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:38.069
debate is burning as bright as his passion,
which I guess is part of the issue. And as

00:00:38.069 --> 00:00:43.170
someone who's favorite character in the story
is Zoro, it would be very easy for me to add

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:50.289
some more fire to the flame. [stop he's already
dead]. However, if I did that, I honestly

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:56.601
would be lying, because to me Sanji is the
most well-written character in all of one

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.601
piece.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:01.100
Hi my name is Manu and even though I don't
smoke - cigarettes - in this video, I will

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:07.760
not only proof to you that Sanji will leave
Wano as a changed man, but also clear his

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.870
and in extension Oda's name, of being a bad
writer when it comes to the man with the curly

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.480
hair - his eyebrows.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.680
My original relationship with Sanji is probably
similar to yours: Pre-time skip Sanji was

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.110
an absolutely fantastic character. He was
not only a true gentleman, but arguably the

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.360
most mature member of the crew, scolding Luffy
for inappropriate behavior, protecting the

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:37.170
weaker members of the crew and even his chivalry
had more of an old-school James-Bond-sort-of

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:46.690
vibe. [Mr. Prince] During that time, deciding
who was my favorite between him Luffy and

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:53.390
Zoro was practically impossible, and also
unnecessary. There was a great balance between

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:58.830
the three, who had very different views, yes,
but nonetheless respected each other, protected

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:03.390
the crew and genuinely deserve the title of
the monster trio.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.740
I guess some people might already have been
uncomfortable with Sanji's outdated views

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:17.180
on women, but it was clearly nothing compared
to after the time skip. I'm not gonna sugarcoat

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:23.520
it, Sanji has been extremely useless and even
worse than that: annoying, ever since the

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.310
straw hats left for fishman island. Through
Punk Hazard, Dressrosa and Zou, while Zoro

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:33.870
and Luffy were getting stronger and stronger,
reaching their full potential, Sanji often

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:39.410
failed to win an important fight and in many
situations, was just cringy to watch for his

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.130
nosebleed horniness.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:45.880
And at that point, I fully agreed with the
people who thought that Oda had ruined Sanji's

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:51.341
great potential, by making him an annoying
and useless joke character. With Whole Cake

00:02:51.341 --> 00:02:57.030
Island however, I was completely shocked,
but mostly relived to find out that this pitiful

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:02.420
version of Sanji I had seen since Fishman
Island, had actually been part of one the

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:15.800
best character arcs, I have ever come across.
And 

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:21.670
the recent developments in Wano have now completely
evaporated my remaining doubts, so I can say

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:28.280
with full confidence that Sanji has not been
ruined. Just the opposite: I believe Oda's

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:34.560
portrayal of our cook, including his over-the-top
perviness, has been very much on purpose and

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.300
will make his growth just the more impactful
once it's complete.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:44.640
One of the fundamental tools for great story
telling and creating a strong main character,

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.489
is the so-called hero's journey that you can
see here on the top RECHTS. And since all

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:54.250
the straw hats are designed as main characters
of their own, this can be applied to each

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:59.030
and everyone of them, which actually would
probably be very interesting to do. Maybe

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.849
I should make a series about that.

00:04:00.849 --> 00:04:06.370
The first step in the heroes journey is the
call to adventure. And Sanji's adventure starts

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:11.840
in the most heartbreaking way possible: He
has to run away from his unloving family that

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.049
has physically and mentally abused him ever
since his mother died, ultimately locking

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:20.400
him in a cage with an iron mask. Getting this
piece of backstory was the first real mind-f''k

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:33.620
moment I had during Whole Cake Island, that
gave so much more context to his character.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:39.330
The second step is meeting a mentor. For Sanji,
this person is of course Zeff. And again,

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:45.190
he has another traumatizing experience, almost
starving to death on an island. However, other

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:50.930
than his family, Zeff actually shows love
for Sanji and is prepared to die for him.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:55.780
It's the first person since his mother that
treats Sanji like a human being and becomes

00:04:55.780 --> 00:05:01.371
his new family, teaching him about cooking
and what it means to be a decent person. Most

00:05:01.371 --> 00:05:06.250
importantly however, he gives Sanji his big
dream, which is to subscribe to Ohara's channel

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:13.080
to get his weekly fix of deep one piece analysis.
That and also to find the all blue.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:18.080
This is where Luffy comes into play. He recruits
Sanji into his crew and gives him a chance

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:24.949
to fulfill his dream. He has now crossed the
threshold and has entered the world of pirates.

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:30.240
And for a while he overcomes his trials pretty
easily. With Mr. Prince, Enies Lobby and his

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:36.150
willingness to take Luffy's pain on Thriller
Bark, Sanji's popularity was at an all time

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:47.000
high. And then the first big failure. Sabaody.
However here it is the crew as a collective

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.490
or arguably Luffy as the captain, that fails
here.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:55.930
And so along everyone else, Sanji grows from
this experience and develops new skills over

00:05:55.930 --> 00:06:03.000
the time skip, which is exactly where Sanji's
downfall in popularity starts. How could that

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:08.259
happen? But will you look at that, it coincides
perfectly with the lowest point of the heroes

00:06:08.259 --> 00:06:11.720
journey: Death and rebirth.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:19.290
As I summarized earlier, Sanji comes out of
the time skip massively flawed: While his

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:25.430
ratio of coolness to pervert was maybe something
like 80:20 before the time skip, to me it

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:31.540
had now shifted to something close to 90:10
on the Pervy end. And I gotta be honest, of

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:36.990
course that would overwrite all the good associations
we have made with him before. And even more

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:42.880
frustrating, he was basically of no use to
the crew anymore. This negative spiral keeps

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:49.110
speeding up until finally, we hit rock! bottom!
with Whole Cake Island, where Sanji not only

00:06:49.110 --> 00:07:06.780
leaves the crew, but even disrespects and
hurts his captain. He is reunited with his

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.930
abusive family who used him as a pawn for
a political marriage and in the end he even

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:17.340
has to learn that his to-be bride Pudding,
the only ray of hope in all of this, actually

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:25.440
had actually been plotting to murder him and
everyone else at the ceremony. [Sanji in the

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.600
rain]

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:31.710
You can see how that's Sanji's lowest point
in the story so far, right? Many people took

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:36.600
this scene as Sanji being heart-broken about
Pudding not loving him, but it's actually

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:42.449
the culmination of his entire character arc
so far literally pouring down on Sanji. And

00:07:42.449 --> 00:07:51.030
the scene reflects that perfectly. Dark alone,
and crying. And this is where everything changes.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:57.199
But to really appreciate Sanji's radical development
from here, you have to understand the main

00:07:57.199 --> 00:08:03.699
point of Sanji's second backstory with the
Vinsmokes, that some people found irrelevant.

00:08:03.699 --> 00:08:07.681
Because Sanji didn't go from awesome to the
state he's in here at Whole Cake island. You

00:08:07.681 --> 00:08:32.050
need to understand, that this is how Sanji
has always seen himself. Right from the very

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:37.560
start, Sanji has had close to no self-worth
as a person. Which really is no big surprise

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.330
given his upbringing. I mean if you got told
you were worthless and treated like an animal

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:46.880
for the first 8 years of your life by your
Nazi family, how would you feel?

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:51.750
Wait what's that on the lens. Oh it's a sponsor,
that's convenient, cause my last video was

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:57.380
expensive. This video is sponsored by Skillshare,
the Sanji of sponsors. Skillshare is an online

